    "result_text": "The full test suite (the single runnable test, `AcceptanceTest`; `AcceptanceBase` is abstract and `AuditLogCapture` is a helper) passes and the build succeeds.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `bulkSignupWarning` flag on the owner responses.\n\n**`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `bulkSignupWarning` boolean to the `Owner` schema (the DTO is code-generated from this spec, giving `OwnerDto` a getter/setter).\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**\n- Added a `BULK_SIGNUP_WARNING_THRESHOLD = 80` constant.\n- In `addOwner`, reused the existing per-day owner count (already computed for the daily-limit check, so no extra query) and set `bulkSignupWarning = ownersRegisteredOnDay > 80` on the response DTO. The count is taken *before* the new owner is saved, matching \"more than 80 owners have **already** been created today.\"\n- In `getOwner`, populated the same field via a small `isBulkSignupDay(...)` helper (count of owners sharing that registration date > 80), so the field is present and correct on reads too \u2014 the acceptance test asserts `$.bulkSignupWarning` is `false` on a fresh `GET`.\n\nBoth paths key off `registrationDate` (rolled to the business day), which is the same accumulation path the daily-limit rule uses \u2014 consistent with the spec and the test's documented expectation. A fresh single create yields `false`; once more than 80 owners share the day it becomes `true`.",
